    response: "The location input field has been successfully enhanced with an autocomplete feature.\n\n**Key Changes:**\n1.  **Unified Input:** Replaced the separate \"Quick Select\" dropdown and manual text input with a single, smart input field.\n2.  **Autocomplete Logic:** As you type, the system now filters the `NORTHWEST_PEAKS` database (from `constants.ts`) to suggest relevant locations.\n3.  **Smart Matching:** The search matches against:\n    *   **Location Name** (e.g., \"T\303\240 X\303\271a\", \"Fansipan\")\n    *   **Aliases/Keywords** (e.g., \"Kh\341\273\247ng Long\", \"N\303\263c nh\303\240 \304\220\303\264ng D\306\260\306\241ng\")\n    *   **Province** (e.g., \"L\303\240o Cai\", \"Y\303\252n B\303\241i\")\n4.  **Rich Suggestions:** The dropdown displays the location name, altitude, province, and relevant aliases to help users choose the correct spot.\n5.  **UX Improvements:** Added click-outside handling to close the dropdown and maintained the existing date range selection functionality."
